/home/sat/mcrl-v025-rank-ws/STATIC-BASELINE-FAMILY-2026-09-10.md:1:**Pooled EE: `RANDOM` 11.233999, `ROUND_ROBIN` 3.441227, `RSS_MAX` 41.621560, `MYOPIC_GREEDY` 28.668530, `NEAREST_ELIGIBLE` parity 11.027760, and `FIRST_IMPROVEMENT_FP` parity 13.430253 Mbit/J; both parity checks reproduced.**
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-rank-ws/STATIC-BASELINE-FAMILY-2026-09-10.md:9:Every arm uses `PANELCEIL`'s frozen global anchors 0–11 in declared order, the complete boundary-0 legal set (visible, D2-eligible, and cell-reachable), the `a-r0` corrected provisioning path, the anchor's declared prior-step incumbent, and singleton evaluation over all 48 realised boundaries. The reported numerator is saturated full-buffer successfully decoded forward-downlink information bits with **no demand cap**. Pooled EE is `sum(bits) / sum(joules)`, never a mean of anchor-local ratios.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-rank-ws/STATIC-BASELINE-FAMILY-2026-09-10.md:11:The service guard has the same scope as in `PANELCEIL`: it filters candidates for objective-based selection (`MYOPIC_GREEDY` and `FIRST_IMPROVEMENT_FP`). A direct static rule is evaluated as selected, even when its realised served count is poor; rejection or resampling would change `RANDOM` from uniform and conceal precisely the below-random outcomes this measurement is meant to expose. All six arms use the same legal-option guard.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-rank-ws/STATIC-BASELINE-FAMILY-2026-09-10.md:19:- **`NEAREST_ELIGIBLE`.** This is the requested parity label for the exact `PANELCEIL` `BASE` construction: reconstruct each frozen anchor's declared carrier mapping at that step, then set a user to null if it has no live legal action. On anchors whose carrier is `nearest-eligible`, that carrier means best D2 margin in the user's own cell with the first valid slot-order tie-break. The 12-anchor panel also deliberately contains `stay-if-possible` and `random-masked` carrier anchors, so the pooled 11.027760 parity value is the carrier-conditioned `BASE`, not a fresh nearest-only reassignment on all 12 rows. This distinction is required to reproduce `PANELCEIL` exactly.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-rank-ws/STATIC-BASELINE-FAMILY-2026-09-10.md:21:- **`MYOPIC_GREEDY`.** Start from that anchor's `PANELCEIL` `BASE` and make exactly one ascending-user sweep. For the current user, hold all other assignments fixed; evaluate the incumbent choice and every legal replacement on **nominal boundary 0** in ordered microbatches of 16; retain candidates whose served-PHY count is at least the initial base count; and choose the largest exact `F = decoded bits - eta_ref * joules`, breaking an exact tie by lexicographically smallest stable configuration ID. Commit the choice immediately for later users. There is no second sweep and no future-boundary selection information.
/home/sat/mcrl-v025-rank-ws/STATIC-BASELINE-FAMILY-2026-09-10.md:23:- **`FIRST_IMPROVEMENT_FP`.** This reruns the certified `PANELCEIL` construction: start from the same base; select on exact **realised boundary-0** `F`; visit ascending users and their declared legal options; accept the first strict improvement meeting the initial base served-PHY guard within ordered microbatches of 16; repeat passes until a complete final pass finds no strict guarded improvement. The 48-boundary result never feeds selection.
